Felucca v1.8.1 – studio twin (firmware code for the host), built from https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca tag v1.8.1
(commit f4df2964649f301ba5abd0ec6000110068672f25; source: https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca/archive/f4df2964649f301ba5abd0ec6000110068672f25.tar.gz),
with its git submodules https://github.com/hugelton/felucca-bsp at commit 5942e68b89ab9ccd23f2c541d712ca38fe635f11 (firmware/bsp), https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca-Engines at commit d0260074ce100a47675814b7f38d61f11176c926 (firmware/engines).
GPL-3.0-only as a whole. Copyright (C) 2026 Leo Kuroshita (@kurogedelic), Hügelton Instruments.
Felucca-Engines (the ANALOG, LOFI, TRIO, WHEEL, NOISE and PHASE engines, dsp.c, felucca_engine.h): MIT; felucca-bsp (the hardware layer: usb.c, ota.c, the board's headers): MPL-2.0, its authors in its NOTICE.
Ported parts keep their licences (msfa in fm6_core.c: Apache-2.0; DaisySP and Rings in phys_dsp.c, phys_symp.c: MIT; the UI face Inter Tight and the Fukiai icons are rasterised in: OFL 1.1, MIT), the instrument samples are CC0
(Versilian Studios): Felucca's LICENSING.md and the texts in THIRD_PARTY.txt beside this file. The JieLi SDK files of Felucca's packages are not part of the twin.
The firmware sources are unmodified. The glue tools/studio/felucca_studio.c (GPL-3.0-only, in FM-1 Companion's source) includes them as Felucca's own browser emulator and host tests do (web/emu/felucca_web.c, tests/hostsim.c,
editor_test.c, backup_test.c) and replaces only the hardware: keys/LEDs/LCD, ADC (MASTER; battery full), NOR flash = a 1 MiB RAM image, USB = always configured (SysEx and MIDI out through usb.c's rings),
one core (MENU > 2ND CORE has no second core here), no key pressure (AFTERTOUCH), no USB audio, no TRS MIDI, no serial console, no updater (ota.c answers the identity handshake only).
Compiled with WASI SDK clang (include shim tools/wasm_shim/sys/wait.h).

Corresponding Source (GNU GPL 3.0, section 6)
The complete corresponding source of this build is https://github.com/hugelton/Felucca at commit f4df2964649f301ba5abd0ec6000110068672f25
together with FM-1 Companion's build script tools/build_sims.py, its submodules named above, the glue tools/studio/felucca_studio.c and the shim tools/wasm_shim. A tarball of exactly this commit
(Felucca-f4df2964649f301ba5abd0ec6000110068672f25.tar.gz, made with tools/make_source_tarballs.py) is attached to every
FM-1 Companion release that ships this build: https://github.com/bit-wmike/fm1-companion/releases
